ve is rough, he must be kind. So, Dave is kind.\n\nNow, let\'s look at point 17: If Dave is kind and rough, then he is quiet. We\'ve established that Dave is both kind and rough, so according to this rule, Dave must be quiet.\n\nWait, but the question is whether "Dave is not quiet" is true. If Dave is quiet, then "Dave is not quiet" would be false. So, the statement is false.\n\nLet me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything. Dave is blue, so he\'s red, which makes him round, hence rough. Rough implies kind. So, Dave is kind and rough, which by rule 17 means he\'s quiet</think>\nTherefore, the option is ']]
